  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/82) by Daniel Catalina (Bitbucket: [Daniel Catalina](https://bitbucket.org/Daniel Catalina), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nI have a strange issue with the Windows builds I create myself following the instructions from Rawpedia: [https://rawpedia.rawtherapee.com/Windows#Clone\\_and\\_build\\_RawTherapee](https://rawpedia.rawtherapee.com/Windows#Clone_and_build_RawTherapee)\n\nBasically, after I open a RAW file \\(does not matter from wich camera\\) it is shown having a red color cast that does not go away no matter what I do. Even using the ‘neutral’ processing profile on an image is causing this.\n\nI’ve attached the AboutThisBuild.txt and a screenshot.\n\nThis does not happen with the builds from: [https://keybase.pub/gaaned92/ART-W64NightlyBuilds/](https://keybase.pub/gaaned92/ART-W64NightlyBuilds/) \\(I tried with ART\\_master\\_1.3-22-g971578cc1\\_W64\\_Skylake\\_200510\\).\n\nThe one major difference between the build that works fine and the one that does not seems to be the gcc version:\n\n* with Compiler: gcc 9.3.0 all is good\n* with Compiler: gcc 10.1.0 the behavior described above can be observed.\n\nI will try to see if I can also use gcc-9 now that I updated MSYS to check if this is really the problem.\n\n‌\n",
